title: Marimo Notebook CVE-2026-39987 Unauthenticated WebSocket RCE
id: 7b6a5c4d-3e2f-1098-bad0-fedcba987654
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects exploitation of CVE-2026-39987, a pre-authentication RCE
    in marimo Python notebook framework. Attackers connect to the
    /terminal/ws WebSocket endpoint which ships without authentication
    in versions through 0.20.4, obtaining an interactive PTY shell.
    This enables rapid credential theft and lateral movement, with
    documented cases of AWS credential extraction in 8 seconds.
references:
  - https://cyberpress.org
  - https://gbhackers.com
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-16
tags:
  - attack.initial-access
  - attack.t1190
  - attack.execution
  - attack.t1059
logsource:
  category: network_connection
  product: linux
detection:
  selection_websocket_endpoint:
    dst_path|contains: '/terminal/ws'
  condition: selection_websocket_endpoint
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate marimo notebook WebSocket connections from authenticated users
level: high
